      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "HDR through a VAE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "VAE Encode (HDR) and VAE Decode (HDR) are a pair. The encoder carries scene-linear HDR into the latent with a log curve (default Compress (Log)) and records it in the latent; the decoder inverts exactly that, so values above 1.0 survive.\n\nUse a linear source (EXR). Pick the VAE your model uses in Load VAE. The Viewer compares the decoded image with the original.\n\nDo not mix these with the stock VAE Encode / VAE Decode."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
